why: run 16 wrote that a constant keeps one part of a type and drops another, which made a value the actor; a value never keeps, drops or rejects, and the note says who is asked about what
labelled: 2026-09-29
--- code
const POSTING_TYPE = 'entry';

export function acceptsEscrow(ledger: Ledger): boolean {
  return ledger.canPost(POSTING_TYPE, 'escrow');
}
--- facts
On the oldest ledgers, `canPost` with a scheme refuses a posting type that carries a currency.
So this constant keeps the posting type and drops the currency.
